      --json            Write one JSON document to stdout; no prompts or animation
  -n, --dry-run         Plan and run read-only steps; skip mutations
  -y, --yes             Accept confirmations (never skips prod)
  -v, --verbose         Stream all child output
  -q, --quiet           Errors and summary only
      --bail            Stop at the first failure
  -t, --track <enum>    internal: TestFlight internal · alpha/beta: TestFlight group · prod: App Store
      --build <number>  Build number (default: max in App Store Connect + 1)
      --notes <string>  Release notes (default: commits since the last ios/v* tag); prod: What's New, required
      --skip <string>   Skip release.preflight checks by skipFlag (comma-separated)

"
`;

exports[`help kit release metadata pull --help 1`] = `
"Download the store listing text into release.<platform>.metadata; --screenshots adds images

Usage
  kit release metadata pull [options]

Examples
  kit release metadata pull ios
  kit release metadata pull android --screenshots
  kit release metadata pull ios --force

Options
  -h, --help         Show help
  -V, --version      Show kit version
      --json         Write one JSON document to stdout; no prompts or animation
  -n, --dry-run      Plan and run read-only steps; skip mutations
  -y, --yes          Accept confirmations (never skips prod)
  -v, --verbose      Stream all child output
  -q, --quiet        Errors and summary only
      --bail         Stop at the first failure
      --screenshots  Also download the screenshots (Play: and the feature graphic and icon)
      --force        Overwrite uncommitted changes in what the pull writes

"
`;

exports[`help kit release metadata push --help 1`] = `
"Upload the store listing text; --screenshots adds images. Never a binary or a review

Usage
  kit release metadata push [options]

Examples
  kit release metadata push ios
  kit release metadata push android --screenshots
  kit release metadata push ios --only-screenshots
  kit release metadata push ios --dry-run
  kit release metadata push android --yes

Options
  -h, --help              Show help
  -V, --version           Show kit version
      --json              Write one JSON document to stdout; no prompts or animation
  -n, --dry-run           Plan and run read-only steps; skip mutations
  -y, --yes               Accept confirmations (never skips prod)
  -v, --verbose           Stream all child output
  -q, --quiet             Errors and summary only
      --bail              Stop at the first failure
      --screenshots       Also replace the screenshots (Play: and the feature graphic and icon)
      --only-screenshots  Replace the screenshots and leave the listing text as the store has it

"
`;

exports[`help kit release promote --help 1`] = `
"Promote a build the store already has to a later track (no rebuild)

Usage
  kit release promote [options]

Examples
  kit release promote android --from alpha --to beta --yes
  kit release promote android --from beta --to prod --rollout 0.2
  kit release promote ios --from beta --to prod --build 42 --notes "Bug fixes"
  kit release promote ios --from beta --to prod --app-version 1.3.0 --build 40 --notes "Hotfix"
  kit release promote ios --from alpha --to beta --dry-run

Options
  -h, --help                  Show help
  -V, --version               Show kit version
      --json                  Write one JSON document to stdout; no prompts or animation
  -n, --dry-run               Plan and run read-only steps; skip mutations
  -y, --yes                   Accept confirmations (never skips prod)
  -v, --verbose               Stream all child output
  -q, --quiet                 Errors and summary only
      --bail                  Stop at the first failure
      --from <string>         Source track: alpha | beta (internal builds are never promoted)
      --to <string>           Destination track, later than --from: beta | prod
      --build <number>        Build number (iOS) or version code (Android); default: the latest on the source track
      --app-version <string>  iOS: version name of the build, when it predates a version bump (default: the TOML version)
      --rollout <number>      Android prod staged-rollout fraction, 0 < r <= 1 (default release.android.prodRollout or 0.1)
      --notes <string>        Release notes; iOS prod: What's New, required (default: the build keeps its notes)
      --draft                 Android: promote as a draft release
      --skip <string>         Skip release.preflight checks by skipFlag (comma-separated)

"
`;

exports[`help kit release rollback --help 1`] = `
"Roll a worker service back to an earlier version (wrangler rollback); tags stay put

Usage
